<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ajele</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Ajele were royal representatives of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alaafin">Alaafin</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oyo-empire">Oyo</a> stationed in tributary towns of the Oyo Empire. They oversaw the collection of tribute and kept the provinces loyal to the capital. Their extractive behaviour generated chronic resentment in the periphery, which contributed to Oyo's later instability.</p></div>
